# Meshy API key. Secret — never commit. Art Forge also reads MESHY_API_KEY.
tools/art-forge/meshy.key

# Raw generator output, wherever it lands. These regenerate in seconds and churn on
# every parameter change, so only approved meshes are committed. Force one in with
# `git add -f` once it has been reviewed.
# Path-independent on purpose: Art Forge defaults its output folder to the source
# image's directory, so sculpts can appear next to the references that made them.
**/*_ai_raw_*.glb
**/*_ai_hi*_*.glb
**/*_ai_v*.glb
**/*_experiment_*.glb

# Explicitly rejected Command Centre material trial. Its Markdown failure record
# is retained, but the 88 MB binary must not be promoted or shipped.
Models/Terran/Buildings/BLD-CMD-001/Base/BLD-CMD-001_base_textured_v01.glb

# Max-quality (no-remesh) source sculpts and their 4K maps. These are the detail
# source you retopo and bake from, not a shippable asset — ~85 MB of mesh plus
# ~50 MB of textures each. Commit the decimated game asset instead.
**/*_hq_*.glb
**/*_hq_*_textures/

# Procedural kit output is deterministic — regenerate with tools/kitgen.py rather than
# committing it. Approved parts get promoted out of _generated/ into the part's own folder.
Kit/**/_generated/

# References hold images only — a mesh in here is a misplaced generator output.
References/**/*.glb
References/**/*.gltf

# Tracker backups — git history is the real backup once a change is committed.
docs/*.BACKUP-*.xlsx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
